{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/773126-weaponizing-pacts","id":773126,"title":"Weaponizing Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-24T08:12:33-08:00","id":773126,"title":"Weaponizing Pacts","content":"1. A Pact can make a mortal rich and powerful.<br /> <br /> 2. All benefits from a Pact must come from somewhere.<br /> <br /> 3. Mortal institutions are concentrations wealth and influence.<br /> <br /> A discussion in the Hunter forum got me thinking of how a demon can derail certain groups indirectly. With a precisely-worded Pact, you could twist an organization to your own ends, at least for a short while.<br /> <br /> For instance, say that you're a demon, and you have a rival who's also a demon. Let's say this rival's name is Moloch, and you're worried Moloch is going to sell you out to the God-Machine. Let's say that Moloch also has an extensive cult.<br /> <br /> So, you find a human dupe and offer him a sweet Pact. One of the many benefits you throw in is dots in Status (Cult of Moloch). All of a sudden you have a plant who is accepted into the fold (at least by the humans; Moloch may get suspicious if he's paying attention, but at that point you tear up the Pact and go hide for a while).<br /> <br /> Or say, a vague yet menacing tech startup has been hunting you for spare parts. Again, find a willing human, maybe one who's amenable to your will, this time make her rich, and word the Pact in such a way that the money comes from being a major shareholder in Utopia Now. Suddenly she is a majority voter in the company's interests. Suddenly you have someone that can shut down a local branch and make them relocate elsewhere. Maybe Alaska.<br /> <br /> I imagine attempting to subvert a supernaturally-invested organization probably invokes a Clash of Wills, and most likely fails outright against supernatural organizations whose existence does not hinge on temporal power (e.g. the Mysterium can't be purchased, since status in the Order is based on mystical knowledge and personal enlightenment, though you might be able to turn a Sleepwalker into a low-ranking mole at least). Also keeping up the ruse probably provokes Compromise rolls eventually, or just some perceptive individual unraveling the deception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T09:12:46-08:00","id":773183,"title":"","content":"I like this idea. It seems legit. I don't know if the Unchained who controls the cult would notice or not though: does it say somewhere if they maintain the memories of the &quot;Prime&quot; timeline even if they're not part of the Pact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T09:25:20-08:00","id":773191,"title":"","content":"I don't quite remember, but I believe that the Unchained's connection to Primum and Infrastructure means that their memories don't get altered the same way normal folk's do. But an inattentive demon with a large cult might not notice one extra member, at first anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:50:11-08:00","id":773398,"title":"","content":"I really like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T06:24:39-08:00","id":773881,"title":"","content":"The only thing I feel is the demon wouldn't have enough control to say exactly where every detail of the pact comes from. They input the in ( to demon) and out (to mortal) of the pact but the steps in-between the system that supports pacts would fill in.<br /> <br /> However giving someone dots in status to have sway over the organization though good for a quick job may not hold up since it only affects memories of those directly effected so there could be gaps that will pop up in long term plans if you go from 0 -100 with your lackey.<br /> <br /> I like the idea though I just I don't feel it'd be a sure shot or that you'd have full control but maybe by being more overt (risking drawing attention) you could force the sources. Like how an exploit is made you force aether through the framework that supports contracts... that opens a whole new can of questions (that requires st approval for anything to happen on the attempt)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T19:37:14-08:00","id":774484,"title":"","content":"I would have issues allowing the demon to direct the pact without any stipulations to do what the demon wants, but I would say there are definitely ways to manipulate a pact to function as a weapon. Like the status one would be a gamble with a random human because all the situations they could gain status in would make it hard to control where it comes from, but a human in the lower ranks of Moloch's cult ,say an initiate, could have status given to them with reasonable confidence that it will be in the cult.<br /> <br /> On the other hand how amicable would everyone be towards a pact where one of the stipulations was damage to the company? Like a bitter business owner making the deal in exchange for a major contract a rival company got that they wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T06:55:39-08:00","id":774755,"title":"","content":"Although it oddly didn't go there in mortal remains, it would seem natural that hunters might even work with demons once they know about the god machine. some Demons might not invoke &quot;threat&quot; to more &quot;moral&quot; hunters, a threat and so they might be willing to make deals, in pursuit of more obvious threats, like vampires. For many less specialized organizations doesn't seem like it would be hard to slip hunter's tips, or perhaps even get a cover of being a hunter by offering to buy out a hunter who wants to retire but has too many enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T09:42:18-08:00","id":774868,"title":"","content":"Using Pacts like this is definitely a gamble; there's a lot of variables involved, plenty of chance for betrayal, incompetence, or misfortune. I suppose if you make it a Soul Pact, then you have the option to get your hands dirty if the mortal asset is screwing things up too much. Other parts might require Storyteller adjudication on whether or not the demon can direct whence comes the Pact's boon. This might not be something many demons do often, but maybe a ring or agency has turned it into their schtick.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I just got a strange notification about this thread: A message saying &quot;-1 others have responded to this post.&quot; When I clicked the link, I got an error screen saying I wasn't authorized to view that page. I think the God-Machine might be onto us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}